[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  february is here yet again but the video  game industry is  still in their winter slumber i was  looking forward to telling you about  outriders a cover shooter crossed with a  looter shooter and also  ryder's republic an extreme sports mmo  and far cry 6's huge return but all  three of those games have been delayed  so we'll talk about them later in the  year with these  aaa games moving aside we can highlight  other games including three  free-to-play games so let's do this  have you heard of little nightmares it's  a puzzled platformer with horror vibes  back in 2017 the original game released  and struggled to find its audience even  though it had many eights and nines out  of ten in review scores  on february 11th the sequel arrives  little nightmares does not include a  single word of dialogue  there are occasional grunts but  everything is experienced through the  actions  of a little girl in a yellow raincoat  this time around she is joined by a boy  wearing a brown bag on his head as a  mask and the two work together  to navigate through pale city the game  is short but this is reflected in the  price point which is less than half the  price of a typical game in most  countries  if you don't think this is the game for  you i urge you to try the free demo out  now  most of the footage right now is from  the 20 minute demo and  instantly you'll get a feel for the  little nightmare's atmosphere which is  so difficult to explain  little nightmares 2 drops on february  11th on playstation xbox switch  and pc  speaking of a dude with a box on his  head next we have a brand's banking new  game  which is being released free on  playstation plus  this is destruction all stars let's get  something out of the way quickly here  destruction all stars is a ps5 exclusive  title which even those on ps4 cannot  play  but if you plan to grab a ps5 in the  future i recommend downloading the  playstation app on your phone  and adding this game to your library  when it releases on february 2nd  it will be waiting for you when you  finally switch to a ps5  no rush the game itself is a destruction  derby of sorts with players smashing  vehicles until a winner is proclaimed  the kicker is each driver is armed with  different abilities  to use to their advantage i have to  admit this looks like a great deal of  fun  but to only release on ps5 with quite a  small user base at the moment  could be a tough start for this game the  art style looks  engaging and fun the characters are  unique and when your car  is vaporized we can run around on foot  sounds like a dreadful idea i can't wait  to try it  releasing on playstation 5 for free on  ps plus on february 2nd  before going full price two months later  let's stick with free games and here's  one that doesn't require an online pass  to access  auto chess remember when auto chess  looked to be taking over the world  and then completely vanished from  existence well it's back again here's  the premise  auto chess is a combination of chess and  tower defense  and mobas yeah it's a weird game genre  but stick with me  you may have already seen the first auto  chess played in star wars by the way  back in the 70s the auto part of the  title is simple too  once the game begins everything is  automated  our job is to build up a deck of  characters to use on the board  which are determined by stats and simply  watch as they scrap  it out the characters have a level of  randomization to add a look element and  focuses us all on knowing  all potential builds of a team to truly  master auto  chess auto chess has been in early  access for about eight months now but on  january 27th  it is in full release on both ps4 and  ps5 completely for free  and it joins mobile and pc versions  they're free as well  there is also a switch version coming  very very soon we are told  could auto chest be the genre you've  been looking for give it a go  it's free after all  about a year ago we looked at a game  called cuisine royale  remember it a battle royale title which  started out as a joke between  friends using pots and pans as armor and  magical boots to leap into the air  well check it out now as of last month  cuisine royale has been revamped  and relaunched as a cursed foad or  cuisine royale second edition  fulfillment of all desires  rolls off the tongue i prefer calling it  christoford the game is going down a  mythical road right now with seasonal  updates which have brought in a thor  style viking  shamans and nuns with rocket launchers  the core game loop remains the same it's  the last person standing wins the game  but as this is a rebrand and a relaunch  i thought i'd spread the word  i personally haven't tried the update  yet please let me know if it's any good  cursed board is available right now on  playstation xbox and pc  [Music]  one last free to play game to get on  your radar this month  roller champions i'll be brief here  there is still no release date past  q1 2021 which means it will be here in  either  march or february as there are so few  games dropping this month  we may see roller champions take  advantage of this lull and release  in february fyi roller champions is a  roller derby style  sports game in which a ball is carried  around and thrown into a goal  more loops round more laps completed and  the ball is worth more points  but all the while the enemy can forcibly  take the ball from you  and score their own goal knowing my luck  this game will be delayed so let's not  dwell on this one right now  but at the moment it's releasing in  february or march  keep an eye out for it  take a look at this werewolf the  apocalypse earthblood  an action role-playing game set in a  sinister world  and as the title suggests we play as a  werewolf  our character can freely change into a  wolf to move around the world quicker  with a lower profile there are three  forms which affect different play styles  the human form is for social and  interaction elements in the world  the wolf form is for exploration and  infiltration  and then there's this form the chronos  form for  combat scenarios and yeah that's the  werewolf you were thinking  about at the start wasn't it kahal is  known as an eco warrior in this world  and looks to expose and close the evil  corporations around the world like the  ones digging for oil  werewolf the apocalypse earthbound  releases on february 4th  on playstation xbox and pc  [Music]  any nintendo fans around here super  mario 3d world and bowser's fury arrive  on february 11th  but you already knew that right it's  more mario what's not to love there and  finally  persona 5 is back again again again the  series which quietly keeps on churning  out content and building up a massive  fan base  this is persona 5 strikers a break from  the core series  strikers is all about hack and slash  action with rpg elements  set six months after the end of persona  5 we follow joker and the phantom  thieves crew as they investigate a  series of strange and compelling  scenarios  and along the way everything will just  become button bashing mayhem  it's great the game released a year ago  in japan  and now on february 23rd the rest of the  world will be able to play this  on ps4 switch and pc  so there we go seven new games coming in  february 2021 we're at the slowest time  of the year for video game releases but  things will be heating up soon with  games like return  and monster hunter rise appearing in  march i'll be back next month to tell  you about those titles  and there's some more free to play games  coming in march so watch this space  i'm adam from playstation grenade you're  awesome i'll see you next time  you

